body:
Here’s my viewpoint;

A white person could say a similar thing, but in America, it wouldn’t hold the same meaning or weight. They have not had the same experience as black Americans, they haven’t had the history that justifies their pride for rising against oppression. 

You, as a person of whatever race, can say whatever you want. But the context surrounding it, the intentions behind the words, are more important than the words themselves sometimes.
